---
// Facts taken from the agents-exe repository README and its polaron.toml.
// The screenshot was supplied by the owner.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import world from '../../assets/agents-world.png';

const REPO = 'https://github.com/jvpts11/agents-exe';
const ALT =
  'The generated world in agents.exe: a river crossing a dry plain, animals scattered over it, and forest on the higher ground';
---

<div class="about agents">
  <div class="about-banner">
    <svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-agents"></use></svg>agents.exe
  </div>
  <div class="about-body">
    <h3 class="about-title">agents.exe</h3>
    <p class="lead">
      A god-game built from nothing: a world that is generated, populated and then left to get on with
      it, while somebody watches. Worldgen, renderer and simulation are all written in Polaron, with no
      engine underneath.
    </p>

    <figure class="shot">
      <Image src={world} alt={ALT} width={460} loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption>Rivers cut the plain, herds graze it, and the forest holds the ridge.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <ul class="chips">
      <li><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-polaron"></use></svg>Written in Polaron</li>
      <li>2560×1440 cells</li>
      <li>17 species</li>
    </ul>

    <fieldset class="group">
      <legend>Status: the ground and the fauna are alive</legend>
      <ul class="devlist">
        <li>Plates, coastlines, climate, rivers, biomes, forests and ore</li>
        <li>About fifteen thousand animals that graze, herd, flee, hunt and starve</li>
        <li>A species can end permanently, and the world says what did it</li>
        <li>The people are next, and after them nations, work and war</li>
      </ul>
    </fieldset>

    <div class="dlg-actions">
      <a class="btn" href="/projects/agents/">Project page</a>
      <a class="btn" href={REPO} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open on GitHub</a>
      <button class="btn" type="button" data-close>Close</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
